                <pb facs="0782" n="698" sameAs="frus:frus1886/pg698"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure in No. 46.—Translation.]</seg></opener>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Judge Castaneda to Mr. Brigham.</hi></head>
                <p>In answer to your favor of this month I have the honor to state to you that all
                    public officers for criminal cases are prohibited by a special law to give any
                    information in regard to the criminal cases that are up before the court to
                    people that have no legal intervention in those cases, the more so when,
                    according to the “International Rights” of Calvo, consuls have no jurisdiction,
                    either civil or criminal, in cases concerning their countrymen. (Book 10,
                    paragraph 490, page 614, volume 1.) All of the above refers to Mr. Cutting, in
                    consequence of which I cannot order his release in any but the forms prescribed
                    by the laws of this country.</p>
                <p>I remain, &amp;c.,</p>
                <closer><signed>R. CASTAÑEDA.</signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
